            <ArticleTitle>[Results of computerized cardio-tomography and radionuclide ventriculography in patients with aortocoronary bypass].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>18-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiocomputer tomography and radionuclide assessment of left ventricular function complete each other in postoperative control of patients with coronary artery bypass grafts. 70 patients with 163 coronary artery bypass grafts had 85% or total bypass graft early postoperative period, 77% after one year and 69% after two years. Sensitivity of cardiocomputer tomography was 75% and accuracy was 84%. The left ventricular functions was unchanged postoperatively.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
